# CivilOS MVP Implementation Plan

## Purpose

This document defines the implementation plan for the first working version of CivilOS.

The MVP must prove that CivilOS can transform an uncertain hypothesis into validated, auditable, reusable, and revisable knowledge.

The MVP is not intended to prove that CivilOS has more agents, more prompts, more screens, or more infrastructure than other AI systems.

The MVP must prove the unique CivilOS value proposition:

> Knowledge validated today can improve an investigation tomorrow.

CivilOS does not compete to generate more answers.

CivilOS exists to create knowledge that can survive evidence review, criticism, validation, memory admission, reuse, challenge, and revision.

---

# Product Hypothesis

Most AI systems follow this pattern:

Question

↓

Answer

↓

Conversation Ends

CivilOS follows a different pattern:

Question

↓

Investigation

↓

Hypotheses

↓

Evidence

↓

Criticism

↓

Independent Validation

↓

Knowledge Record

↓

Persistent Memory

↓

Future Reuse

↓

