# MVP Exit Criteria

CivilOS MVP is complete only when all the following are true:

- A real question creates an Investigation.
- The Investigation creates one or more Hypotheses.
- Evidence remains traceable to real Sources.
- Criticism occurs before acceptance.
- An authoritative Validation Decision exists.
- Memory Admission occurs separately.
- An active Knowledge Record is created.
- The Knowledge Record remains available after the Investigation ends.
- A later Investigation retrieves and actually reuses the Knowledge Record.
- A Knowledge Reuse Record proves the reuse.
- New Evidence can challenge the Knowledge Record.
- Revalidation can create a new Knowledge Revision.
- Previous versions remain available.
- Trust comes from recorded outcomes.
- Graph relationships remain evidence-backed.
- Important actions remain auditable.
- Provider failure creates no fake activity.
- Every displayed metric comes from recorded activity.
- The three-part proof experience works with real backend state.

If Knowledge Creation, Reuse, and Evolution do not all work, the MVP is not complete.

---

# Stop Conditions

Implementation must pause feature expansion when:

- The vertical slice is incomplete.
- Data integrity fails.
- Audit lineage breaks.
- Knowledge cannot be reused.
- Revision destroys history.
- The UI displays unrecorded state.
- Provider unavailability creates pressure to fabricate outputs.
- Scope expansion threatens the core proof.

The correct response is to repair the core, not add more features.

---

# Final Product Proof

CivilOS proves its value when the system can truthfully show:

```text
Investigation 1 created validated Knowledge K001.

Investigation 2 reused K001.

Investigation 3 challenged and improved K001.

Every step remains supported by evidence, validation, versions, and audit history.
```

This is knowledge compounding.

This is the CivilOS MVP.

